[
{ type: install
  message: <<EOM
Stalwart Proxy has been installed as %%PREFIX%%/bin/stalwart-proxy.

1. Edit %%ETCDIR%%/config.toml (destinations, listeners,
   TLS certificates) and %%ETCDIR%%/mappings.tsv.
   Additional example configurations are available in
   %%EXAMPLESDIR%%.

2. Create the admin API token referenced by [admin].bearer_token_file:

     umask 027
     openssl rand -hex 32 > %%ETCDIR%%/admin.token
     chgrp %%GROUPS%% %%ETCDIR%%/admin.token

3. The proxy runs as the unprivileged user "%%USERS%%" but the
   sample configuration listens on privileged ports (< 1024).
   Either allow this user to bind them with mac_portacl(4):

     sysrc kld_list+=mac_portacl
     kldload mac_portacl
     sysctl net.inet.ip.portrange.reservedlow=0
     sysctl net.inet.ip.portrange.reservedhigh=0
     sysctl security.mac.portacl.rules=uid:485:tcp:25,uid:485:tcp:110,uid:485:tcp:143,uid:485:tcp:443,uid:485:tcp:465,uid:485:tcp:587,uid:485:tcp:993,uid:485:tcp:995

   (add the sysctls to /etc/sysctl.conf to make them persistent),
   or run the proxy as root with stalwart_proxy_user="root".

4. Enable and start the service:

     sysrc stalwart_proxy_enable=YES
     service stalwart_proxy start

The proxy logs to /var/log/stalwart-proxy.log by default.
EOM
}
]
